; With a prefix, it asks for that many lines, the other way when
; negative; with -, a page the other way, as Emacs's C-v takes them. A
; forward step is asked twice here, the page first answering more.
> (define steps '())
> (define (note-step ask client name value)
    (set! steps (cons (map (lambda (key) (cdr (assoc key value))) '("forward" "by")) steps))
    (ask client name value))
